window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-051.json",{"day":51,"title":"The Real Price of a Neighborhood Shop","targetWords":[{"word":"cost","gloss":"成本","context":"When a neighborhood shop raised the cost of bread, residents debated whether the new price was fair.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"price","gloss":"价格","context":"When a neighborhood shop raised the cost of bread, residents debated whether the new price was fair.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"buy","gloss":"购买","context":"Some decided to buy elsewhere without asking how the product reached the shelf.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"product","gloss":"产品","context":"Some decided to buy elsewhere without asking how the product reached the shelf.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"benefit","gloss":"益处","context":"Others considered the benefit of a nearby shop for people unable to travel far.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"market","gloss":"市场","context":"A market can reflect both production expenses and the choices of sellers, so neither affection nor suspicion alone explains it.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"industry","gloss":"行业","context":"The food industry faced a higher interest rate, and stories about a million dollars in investment did not reveal the position of a small retailer.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"rate","gloss":"比率","context":"The food industry faced a higher interest rate, and stories about a million dollars in investment did not reveal the position of a small retailer.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"million","gloss":"百万","context":"The food industry faced a higher interest rate, and stories about a million dollars in investment did not reveal the position of a small retailer.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"value","gloss":"价值","context":"The value of the shop to the local economy involved more than one visible number.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"economy","gloss":"经济","context":"The value of the shop to the local economy involved more than one visible number.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"percent","gloss":"百分之","context":"A five percent increase in rent affected every customer, yet he could not sell enough additional bread merely by keeping the old price.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"customer","gloss":"顾客","context":"A five percent increase in rent affected every customer, yet he could not sell enough additional bread merely by keeping the old price.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sell","gloss":"出售","context":"A five percent increase in rent affected every customer, yet he could not sell enough additional bread merely by keeping the old price.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"store","gloss":"商店","context":"The store did not make him rich, though residents were right to ask about the amount of his income.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rich","gloss":"富有的","context":"The store did not make him rich, though residents were right to ask about the amount of his income.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"account","gloss":"账目","context":"The owner published a simple account of his current expenses.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"amount","gloss":"数量","context":"The store did not make him rich, though residents were right to ask about the amount of his income.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"income","gloss":"收入","context":"The store did not make him rich, though residents were right to ask about the amount of his income.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"current","gloss":"当前的","context":"The owner published a simple account of his current expenses.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sale","gloss":"销售","context":"A large sale might help clear goods before they spoiled.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"trade","gloss":"贸易","context":"Meanwhile, wholesale trade, transport, and tax all influenced the final bill.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"tax","gloss":"税","context":"Meanwhile, wholesale trade, transport, and tax all influenced the final bill.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"billion","gloss":"十亿","context":"National figures measured in a billion units gave little guidance about whether one street could support a shop that opened early, offered credit cautiously, and knew which residents needed delivery.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"credit","gloss":"赊购","context":"National figures measured in a billion units gave little guidance about whether one street could support a shop that opened early, offered credit cautiously, and knew which residents needed delivery.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"bill","gloss":"账单","context":"Meanwhile, wholesale trade, transport, and tax all influenced the final bill.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"charge","gloss":"收费","context":"A small delivery charge did not necessarily represent an unreasonable profit.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"profit","gloss":"利润","context":"A small delivery charge did not necessarily represent an unreasonable profit.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"balance","gloss":"余额","context":"It could pay a driver's time, provided that the owner kept a transparent balance between expenses and revenue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"dollar","gloss":"美元","context":"For a family counting every dollar, however, each purchase still mattered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"purchase","gloss":"购买","context":"For a family counting every dollar, however, each purchase still mattered.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"fund","gloss":"资助","context":"The council considered whether to fund a shared delivery route rather than hand money to an individual business.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wealth","gloss":"财富","context":"Public wealth should support an identifiable need.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"cheap","gloss":"便宜的","context":"A cheap loaf from a distant factory might suit many households, but its price did not include the difficulty faced by someone unable to reach it.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"factory","gloss":"工厂","context":"A cheap loaf from a distant factory might suit many households, but its price did not include the difficulty faced by someone unable to reach it.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"expense","gloss":"开支","context":"A useful comparison therefore examined access as well as the expense printed on a label.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"debt","gloss":"债务","context":"The owner carried debt from equipment purchased to manufacture a few basic items on site.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"manufacture","gloss":"制造","context":"The owner carried debt from equipment purchased to manufacture a few basic items on site.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"gift","gloss":"礼物","context":"A supplier's apparent gift was actually a promotional arrangement with conditions attached.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"cent","gloss":"美分","context":"Saving one cent per unit could matter across a year's sales, but the household budget was not identical to the business budget.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"budget","gloss":"预算","context":"Saving one cent per unit could matter across a year's sales, but the household budget was not identical to the business budget.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"brand","gloss":"品牌","context":"A familiar brand did not guarantee better quality.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"ticket","gloss":"票","context":"Nor should a discount ticket or a promised prize distract shoppers from comparing ordinary prices.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"prize","gloss":"奖品","context":"Nor should a discount ticket or a promised prize distract shoppers from comparing ordinary prices.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"stock","gloss":"库存","context":"The shop needed enough stock for regular demand while avoiding waste.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"recession","gloss":"衰退","context":"During a recession, it would be particularly risky to assume that every loyal visitor could continue spending the same amount.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"gold","gloss":"金","context":"There was no pot of gold waiting in the accounts.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"revenue","gloss":"收入","context":"It could pay a driver's time, provided that the owner kept a transparent balance between expenses and revenue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"welfare","gloss":"福利","context":"The town's welfare depended on an exchange that residents and sellers could understand.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"exchange","gloss":"交换","context":"The town's welfare depended on an exchange that residents and sellers could understand.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a neighborhood shop raised the cost of bread, residents debated whether the new price was fair. Some decided to buy elsewhere without asking how the product reached the shelf. Others considered the benefit of a nearby shop for people unable to travel far. A market can reflect both production expenses and the choices of sellers, so neither affection nor suspicion alone explains it. The food industry faced a higher interest rate, and stories about a million dollars in investment did not reveal the position of a small retailer. The value of the shop to the local economy involved more than one visible number.","zh":"社区商店提高面包成本时，居民争论新价格是否公平。一些人决定去别处买，却不询问产品怎样来到货架上。另一些人考虑附近商店对无法远行者的益处。市场能反映生产费用与卖家选择，因此仅凭喜爱或怀疑都无法解释。食品行业面临更高利率，而关于百万美元投资的报道，不能说明小零售商的处境。商店对当地经济的价值涉及不止一个显眼数字。"},{"en":"The owner published a simple account of his current expenses. A five percent increase in rent affected every customer, yet he could not sell enough additional bread merely by keeping the old price. The store did not make him rich, though residents were right to ask about the amount of his income. A large sale might help clear goods before they spoiled. Meanwhile, wholesale trade, transport, and tax all influenced the final bill. National figures measured in a billion units gave little guidance about whether one street could support a shop that opened early, offered credit cautiously, and knew which residents needed delivery.","zh":"店主公布了一份当前开支的简单账目。租金上涨百分之五影响每位顾客，但维持旧价格本身并不能多卖出足够面包。商店没有让他富有，不过居民有权询问收入数额。大促销也许能在变质前清掉货物。与此同时，批发贸易、运输和税收都会影响最终账单。以十亿为单位的全国数字，对一条街能否支撑一家早开门、谨慎允许赊购，并了解哪些住户需要送货的商店，指导作用很小。"},{"en":"A small delivery charge did not necessarily represent an unreasonable profit. It could pay a driver's time, provided that the owner kept a transparent balance between expenses and revenue. For a family counting every dollar, however, each purchase still mattered. The council considered whether to fund a shared delivery route rather than hand money to an individual business. Public wealth should support an identifiable need. A cheap loaf from a distant factory might suit many households, but its price did not include the difficulty faced by someone unable to reach it. A useful comparison therefore examined access as well as the expense printed on a label.","zh":"少量配送费不一定代表不合理利润。只要店主透明地平衡支出与收入，它就可能用于支付司机时间。但对每一美元都要精打细算的家庭来说，每次购买仍重要。议会考虑资助共同配送路线，而非把钱直接交给单一企业。公共财富应支持明确需求。远方工厂的便宜面包也许适合许多家庭，但价格没有包括无法去那里购买者的困难。有用的比较因此要同时检查获取途径，以及标签上印出的费用。"},{"en":"The owner carried debt from equipment purchased to manufacture a few basic items on site. A supplier's apparent gift was actually a promotional arrangement with conditions attached. Saving one cent per unit could matter across a year's sales, but the household budget was not identical to the business budget. A familiar brand did not guarantee better quality. Nor should a discount ticket or a promised prize distract shoppers from comparing ordinary prices. The shop needed enough stock for regular demand while avoiding waste. During a recession, it would be particularly risky to assume that every loyal visitor could continue spending the same amount.","zh":"店主为了购买设备、现场制作几种基本食品而背负债务。供应商看似赠送的礼物，实际上是附带条件的促销安排。每件节省一美分，全年可能有意义，但家庭预算并不等于企业预算。熟悉品牌不保证更好品质。折扣券或承诺的奖品也不应让顾客忘记比较正常价格。商店需要足够库存满足日常需求，同时避免浪费。经济衰退期间，假定每位忠实顾客都能继续花同样的钱，尤其危险。"},{"en":"There was no pot of gold waiting in the accounts. Nevertheless, a reasonable revenue could support wages and keep a useful service open. The town's welfare depended on an exchange that residents and sellers could understand. The owner agreed to explain major price changes, while a community group arranged deliveries for households facing the greatest barriers. Not everyone returned to the shop, and that was their right. The discussion succeeded because it replaced a simple argument about greedy sellers and careless buyers with evidence about costs, needs, and alternatives. Fairness became a question that people could examine together, rather than a slogan attached to a price.","zh":"账目里没有等待发掘的金山。然而合理收入可以支付工资，让有用服务继续开放。小镇的福祉依赖于居民和卖家都能理解的交换。店主同意解释主要价格变化，社区组织则为障碍最大的家庭安排配送。并非每个人都回到这家店，那是他们的权利。讨论的成功在于，它用关于成本、需要和替代选择的证据，取代了对贪婪卖家和粗心买家的简单争论。公平成为人们能共同探究的问题，而非贴在价格上的口号。"}],"previous":50,"next":52});
